    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0221" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg119"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 14911/9–10.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic">November 21,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 125.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 17th instant, with which was inclosed a copy of a cablegram
                    forwarded to you by the Wai-wu Pu from His Imperial Majesty, the Emperor of
                    China, to the President, announcing the demise of His Imperial Majesty, the late
                    Emperor of China.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the message inclosed in your
                    communication has been transmitted to the President and that the American
                    minister at Peking has been instructed to present a telegram of condolence and
                    sympathy from the President to His Imperial Majesty.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
